    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe specification required all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) to return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body carrying `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`.\n\n**What I found:** The OfficeFloor Spring Boot starter bridges responses through Spring MVC's message converters (via `RequestMappingHandlerAdapter`), so returning a `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>` makes Spring automatically emit `application/problem+json`. Several escalation handlers (validation-400, data-integrity, forbidden, general) already used this `ProblemDetail` pattern via the existing `ProblemDetails.build(...)` helper \u2014 but the nine business-rule rejection handlers still returned an ad-hoc `Map.of(\"errors\", ...)` body serialized as plain `application/json`.\n\n**What I changed** \u2014 converted these nine handlers to the `ProblemDetail` pattern:\n\n- 400: `MissingOwnerFields`, `DisposableEmailDomain`, `FutureRegistrationDate`, `InvalidEmail`, `InvalidPostcode`, `InvalidTelephone`\n- 409: `CityAtCapacity`, `DuplicateIdentity`\n- 429: `DailyOwnerLimit`\n\nEach now builds a `ProblemDetail` via `ProblemDetails.build(ex, status, detail)` (which sets `type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`) and preserves the prior field-level info as an extra `errors` property so no information is lost. HTTP status codes are unchanged.\n\n**Verification:** confirmed the baseline failure of the new `Cp59Tests` (was `application/json`), then the full suite \u2014 71 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
